<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mawali</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The mawali were non-Arab converts to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphates</a>, attached as clients to Arab tribes. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> they often faced discrimination in taxation and status despite conversion. Their grievances, especially in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a>, fed support for the Abbasid revolution that overthrew the Umayyads.</p></div>
